  "notes": "{否決|ひけつ} means to reject a proposal or bill by vote. Combines {否|ひ} (negate) + {決|けつ} (decide).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {法案|ほうあん}を{否決|ひけつ}する: to vote down a bill\n- {反対|はんたい}{多数|たすう}で{否決|ひけつ}: rejected by majority opposition\n- {満場|まんじょう}{一致|いっち}で{否決|ひけつ}: rejected unanimously\n- {否決|ひけつ}{権|けん}: veto power\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {可決|かけつ}: passage, approval (antonym) — {否決|ひけつ} and {可決|かけつ} form a natural pair\n- {却下|きゃっか}: rejection, dismissal — used in legal/administrative contexts, not necessarily by vote\n- {棄却|ききゃく}: dismissal — primarily legal (e.g., dismissing a case)\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal. Used in political, parliamentary, and corporate governance contexts.",
